  address = {London},
  note = {
  CORE ARGUMENT: Anderson surveys the major figures of Western
  Marxism from Lukacs through Althusser and Colletti, arguing that
  the tradition's defining characteristic is its displacement from
  political economy and revolutionary practice to aesthetic and
  philosophical speculation. This displacement was produced by the
  defeat of the European working class movements of the 1920s-30s;
  Western Marxism is thus a Marxism of defeat, whose philosophical
